content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Postal Clerk",
      "description": "Employee who receives packages and calculates postage"
    },
    {
      "name": "Package",
      "description": "Physical parcel submitted by a customer",
      "attributes": [
        "Receipt",
        "Weight"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Receipt",
      "description": "Proof that a package was accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "Weight",
      "description": "Measured weight of a package"
    },
    {
      "name": "Postage",
      "description": "Calculated cost for sending a package"
    },
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "description": "Person sending or receiving mail"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sorting Officer",
      "description": "Employee who sorts mail and prepares delivery batches"
    },
    {
      "name": "Mail",
      "description": "Grouped postal items prepared for routing",
      "attributes": [
        "Package",
        "Location"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Location",
      "description": "Current place of a mail item"
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery Batch",
      "description": "Collection of mail prepared for a delivery route",
      "attributes": [
        "Mail"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Route",
      "description": "Planned path for delivering a delivery batch",
      "attributes": [
        "Delivery Batch",
        "Delivery Status"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery Status",
      "description": "Progress update for a delivery"
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery Carrier",
      "description": "Worker who transports and delivers mail"
    },
    {
      "name": "Shipping Form",
      "description": "Form completed by a customer to initiate a shipment"
    },
    {
      "name": "Receipt Confirmation",
      "description": "Customer confirmation that mail was received"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Shipping": {
      "objects": [
        "Customer",
        "Postal Clerk",
        "Package",
        "Receipt",
        "Weight",
        "Postage",
        "Shipping Form"
      ]
    },
    "Distribution": {
      "objects": [
        "Delivery Carrier",
        "Customer",
        "Route",
        "Receipt Confirmation"
      ]
    },
    "Mail Organisation": {
      "objects": [
        "Sorting Officer",
        "Delivery Batch",
        "Mail",
        "Location"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- In case an object appears in multiple bounded contexts, suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Shipping": {
      "derived from": "Shipping Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Sender",
        "Postal Clerk",
        "Package",
        "Receipt",
        "Weight",
        "Postage",
        "Shipping Form"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Customer -> Sender"
      ]
    },
    "Distribution": {
      "derived from": "Distribution Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Delivery Carrier",
        "Recipient",
        "Route",
        "Receipt Confirmation"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Customer -> Recipient"
      ]
    },
    "Mail Organisation": {
      "derived from": "Mail Organisation Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Sorting Officer",
        "Delivery Batch",
        "Mail",
        "Location"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    }
  }
}
```
